--TEST--
A `Core\Csv::rows` cell read from an upload part is a `tainted string`, so a plain `string` variable does not take it — `rule:core-api/a-member-takes-the-source-the-program-holds`, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The rows read the part's bytes, so every cell carries the part's taint.
foreach (Core\Request::files() as Core\Request\Part $part) {
    foreach (Core\Csv::rows($part) as var $record) {
        tainted string $held = $record["0"];
        string $name = $record["0"];
        echo $held, $name, "\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:6:24
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
